@startuml
title MountSession Lifecycle

[*] --> NoSessions : app starts

state NoSessions {
  NoSessions : do / await open action
}

state HasSessions {
  [*] --> Browsing

  state Browsing {
    Browsing : do / display session tree;\nrespond to file selection
  }

  state Operating {
    Operating : entry / start background task
    Operating : do / execute file operation\n(extract, delete, copy, paste, rename)
    Operating : exit / report result to user
  }

  state Saving {
    Saving : do / repack archive from temp\ndirectory to original file on disk
  }

  Browsing  --> Operating : file operation triggered
  Operating --> Browsing  : operation complete or failed
  Browsing  --> Saving    : save archive requested
  Saving    --> Browsing  : save complete
}

NoSessions  --> HasSessions : session opened\n(archive, directory, or remote mount)
HasSessions --> HasSessions : another session opened or active session switched
HasSessions --> NoSessions  : last session closed
HasSessions --> [*]         : app exits\n(open archive sessions flushed)
NoSessions  --> [*]         : app exits

note right of HasSessions
  Multiple sessions may be open simultaneously.
  Opening another archive adds a new session
  rather than replacing the current one.
  Archive sessions are flushed on close;
  directory and remote mounts are write-through.
end note
@enduml
